        "is_free": false,
        "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >TO BE CLEAR: YOU NEED TO BE SOMEWHAT FAMILIAR WITH HOW PROGRAMMING WORKS IN ORDER TO ENJOY THIS GAME.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >1-DC is an open-ended programming puzzle game (a &quot;zach-like&quot;), featuring a fictional low-level programming language. There are only three base commands; the rest depends on the commands' parameters (somewhat like SIC-1). This challenges the player to think in abstract and minimal terms.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >How can you calculate a sine wave with only two variables? That's up to you to figure out.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >32 base levels;</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >16 bonus levels, featuring negative numbers and a third variable slot;</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A commands par in each level that you can optimize for;</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >12 achievements, ranging from tedious to confusing;</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A simple level editor, with more variable slots and a greater range of values</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Voicelogs left by your boss, to inform you about his search for your missing wife.</p></li></ul>",
        "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >TO BE CLEAR: YOU NEED TO BE SOMEWHAT FAMILIAR WITH HOW PROGRAMMING WORKS IN ORDER TO ENJOY THIS GAME.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >1-DC is an open-ended programming puzzle game (a &quot;zach-like&quot;), featuring a fictional low-level programming language. There are only three base commands; the rest depends on the commands' parameters (somewhat like SIC-1). This challenges the player to think in abstract and minimal terms.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >How can you calculate a sine wave with only two variables? That's up to you to figure out.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >32 base levels;</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >16 bonus levels, featuring negative numbers and a third variable slot;</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A commands par in each level that you can optimize for;</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >12 achievements, ranging from tedious to confusing;</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A simple level editor, with more variable slots and a greater range of values</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Voicelogs left by your boss, to inform you about his search for your missing wife.</p></li></ul>",
        "short_description": "An open-ended programming puzzle game with a minimalist, abstract, Assembly-like programming language.",
